Subject: [#94-9-590] Quality of Interface

Subject: Re: Quality of Interface



The state of mind could be described as the quality of the interface.......

The interface not between the mind and the outside world but the mind
itself . The clearer the mind the clearer the interface.
If this model is applied to everyday activities "real or virtual" the
benefit is already gained . This can be explained for example by
imagining riding a bike or car . Clearly the early stages of learning to
drive are cluttered with the remembering of controls or manoeuvres . The
action of driving is broken up in to separate sections : steering , gears
and observations etc , But as the user becomes more experienced , and
this can be be applied to a user of any description, the separate
sections merge together.The gap between wanting to drive and driving is
fused , the act of driving becomes a mental state rather then a physical
action or rather the physical+mental states are united.The boundary
between mind and machine is fused and hence the interface is made obsolete
This can be described as the non existent interface . A state that is the
most valuable and desired , this is the quality  of the interface - to fuse
and join to be aware and alert .

If the interface is seen as that which lets human interact with
 machine then this also leads to the interface as the mind .
If the current progress continues then how long shall it be before the
mouse, dataglove and headset are replaced with technology,
directly linked to the brain.If these technologies become realised the
use of them will involve clear thinking,alertness and an exceptance to flow.
This would lead to the interface as being a conscious decision both
physically and mentally and the Quality of the interface would be the
quality of mind.

Im currently writing a 5000 word paper and would appreciate input from
people with opinions B-).......   lbarnard@gwent.ac.uk 


